;; Python's read level's divergences (bin/reap's [:python :read], queue 201 PY10; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, "As built:
;; PY10"): the classes of repr/python's known files at that level, test/python/roundtrip-known.edn (the round trip's :lines
;; levels, PY2), lex-check-known.edn and parse-check-known.edn (the native reader, PY9), and beside it pyi's front end's
;; scope-known.edn and compile-known.edn (PY5a, empty), in test/goi/divergences.edn's format (C8's way: from the known
;; files' :classes). A case is "CORPUS FILE" (scope's and compile's "CHECK/CORPUS FILE"), its reason "known CLASS: the
;; class's text" (bin/reap's c-known reader). A class a known file gains is added here by hand, with its kind and decision.
;; Read with the Clojure reader.
[
 {:id :rejected
  :title "CPython rejects the file; the read is judged on its class and message"
  :kind :design
  :why "a deliberately bad file of Lib/test (an unknown or wrong encoding, a character no identifier takes): ast.parse rejects it, the read gives (python/error CLASS MSG ...) with CPython's class and message, nothing to print (survey §5.3)"
  :decided "PYS3 (a) (the user, 2026-11-03); PY2"
  :match [#"^known rejected:"]}
 {:id :code-lines
  :title ":lines: the forms and the ast equal, the code compiled from the print not (its positions)"
  :kind :design
  :why "CPython 3.14's code generation depends on the lines a node spans beyond what tools/pydump's code_digest normalizes (exception ranges, jumps, LOAD_FAST fusion); :lines carries no lines; the same files pass every level in :full (PY3)"
  :decided "queue 175's DECISION (a) (the user, 2026-11-03)"
  :match [#"^known code-lines:"]}
 {:id :charset
  :title "an encoding the runtime has no charset for (KOI8-R)"
  :kind :design
  :why "jrt's charsets are the root/English set of the locales decision of 2026-10-11: Lib/test's module_koi8_r.py cannot be decoded (the lexer) or written back (the print)"
  :decided "queue 176's DECISION (a) (the user, 2026-11-03); empty since py-design-1122 (2026-11-21): jrt has ISO-8859-7 and the reader names it (test_exceptions' coding spec iso8859-7 decodes, its case judged by its own verdict); KOI8-R read since before"
  :match [#"^known charset:"]}
 {:id :error-message
  :title "the native parser rejects what CPython rejects, with another message or position"
  :kind :deferred
  :owner "PY9 (PY9c: pegen's second pass, the invalid_ rules, pegen_errors.c's messages)"
  :why "the native parser's first-pass failure is reported as \"invalid syntax\" at the last token read; CPython's error passes are PY9c's"
  :decided "PY9b's scope (the coordinator, queue 199)"
  :match [#"^known error-message:"]}
 {:id :helper-error
  :title "the helper (tools/pydump) itself fails on the file: the native reader is not judged on it"
  :kind :design
  :why "a mutant with a lone CR inserted on which pydump.py tree --full fails: no reference to judge the native reader against (the mutants are not counted by bin/reap, as C's)"
  :decided "PY9b, by rule"
  :match [#"^known helper-error:"]}
 {:id :helper-debug-comment
  :title "a debug field's expression holds a comment: the reference (tools/pydump) keeps it, CPython and the native reader drop it"
  :kind :deferred
  :owner "tools/pydump.py's _field (the oracle's debug text: every comment of the field's text dropped, strings respected, as lexer.c's set_ftstring_expr), then the records made again; DECISION 1 of queue 428"
  :why "Lib/test's test_fstring.py and test_tstring.py (a field (1,  # Force lexer metadata reconstruction. ...)= in a triple-quoted f-string and t-string): ast.parse's debug Constant has no comment (probed on CPython 3.14.10, queue 428), the native reader's :debug neither; the helper strips comments only around the expression's own span"
  :decided "proposed by queue 428 (the helper's, not the reader's), decision pending: the user's"
  :match [#"^known helper-debug-comment:"]}
 {:id :own-traceback
  :title "syntax-errors: the case's own verdict is a doctest's exception line with traceback's keyword suggestion"
  :kind :design
  :why "test_syntax's doctest expects format_exception_only's line, to which traceback.py adds the keyword typo's suggestion (\"invalid syntax. Did you mean 'for'?\"); the reader's message is the parser's and the record agrees with it; the suggestion is judged where test_syntax runs (bin/pyi check)"
  :decided "by design (queue 240; queue 245); empty since py-design-1122 (2026-11-21): parse-check's own verdict judges a doctest's line as format_exception_only gives it, Lib/traceback.py's _find_keyword_typos ported (arbace.repr.python.parsecheck's keyword-typo: suggestions.c's Levenshtein, difflib's close matches, codeop's compile_command with pyi's own compiler for its final compile)"
  :match [#"^known own-traceback:"]}
 {:id :own-mode
  :title "syntax-errors: the case's own verdict is the error of another mode (eval)"
  :kind :design
  :why "test_fstring's assertAllRaise evaluates its cases (mode eval), where CPython's parser reports another error than in exec mode; the reader reads in exec mode as ast.parse does and the record agrees with it; the test's eval mode is judged under pyi (bin/pyi check)"
  :decided "by design (queue 240; queue 245); empty since py-design-1122 (2026-11-21): each expectation is judged on the error of its own mode (assertAllRaise's eval, eval()'s leading blanks stripped; a doctest's single)"
  :match [#"^known own-mode:"]}
]
